{"id":"H1807","lemma":"דְּלִילָה","transliteration":"delilah","sayIt":"de-li-LAH","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Delilah","meaning":"A woman living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jdg.16.4; married to Samson (H8123)\n§ Delilah = \"feeble\"\nthe Philistine mistress of Samson who betrayed the secret of his great strength, and by cutting his hair, enfeebled him and delivered him to the Philistines","glosses":["so delilah","then delilah","delilah","when delilah"],"count":6,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"was Delilah"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"So Delilah","kjv":"And Delilah"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Then Delilah","kjv":"And Delilah"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"So Delilah","kjv":"Delilah"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"Then Delilah","kjv":"And Delilah"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-16","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"When Delilah","kjv":"And when Delilah"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Judges 16:4","note":"It came to pass afterward that he loved a woman in the valley of Sorek, whose name was Delilah.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H8123","lemma":"שִׁמְשׁוֹן","transliteration":"shimshon","gloss":"Samson"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}